meta {
  name: Delete the draft copy
  type: http
  seq: 29
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/curricula/{{curriculumCopyId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 204
}

docs {
  The draft is abandoned rather than kept, so this is a delete and not an
  archive. Archiving is for a syllabus that was taught and needs to stay
  readable next to the marks it produced; deleting is for one that never was.

  Deleting a curriculum takes its nodes with it -- they have no meaning apart
  from it -- but it stops dead at a placement. Both the curriculum and its
  nodes are named by placement rows that refuse to be orphaned, so a syllabus
  content has been mapped to cannot be dropped without someone first deciding
  what happens to the mapping.

  The curriculum the rest of the run uses stays behind for folder 12.
}
